<title>USA: Greenwich Air gets $28 mln in contracts.</title>
<headline>Greenwich Air gets $28 mln in contracts.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI, Fla. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greenwich Air Services Inc said on Wednesday it has signed seven new contracts in the past month to overhaul and repair a variety of airplane engines.</p>
<p>Six, one-year contracts are worth an estimated $16 million in the next year, the company said.</p>
<p>A seventh contract with  Qatar Airways to repair and overhaul CF6 engines at the company's Caledonian subsidiary in Scotland is worth an estimated $12 million over three years, the company said.  </p>
<p>The other six contracts are with Alfa Romeo for Alitalia ; the Royal Moroccan Air Force; McDonnell Douglas Lease Finance;  U.S. Turbine Engine Corp ; Midway ; and the United States Air Force.</p>
